# What never belongs in a deployment archive.
#
# `vercel --archive=tgz` tars the working directory, and it does not read
# .gitignore -- so anything a local tool happens to be writing at that moment
# goes up with the source. Playwright's trace directory is the one that bites:
# a deploy run while the browser suite is running fails outright with
#
#   Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, lstat
#   'test-results/.playwright-artifacts-0/traces/resources/<hash>.htc'
#
# because Playwright deletes those files between tests, in the window between
# the archiver listing the directory and reading it. Nothing here is needed to
# build the app, so the fix is to leave it all behind rather than to avoid
# deploying and testing at the same time.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# Local QA output. Large, regenerated per run, and of no use to the build.
qa-*.json
qa-report-print.html
Onyx-LMS-QA-Certification.pdf

# Build and dependency caches. Vercel installs and builds from source.
node_modules/
.next/
apps/web/.next/
packages/*/dist/

# Local environment and database dumps.
.env
.env.*
backups/
